.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-RECOVERY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-recovery
.Nd find and import a broken machine's pools from the live image, leaving virtual machines' pools alone
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm import | scan | list-pools | list-datasets
.Nm
.Op Cm help | Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The first step in repairing a machine that will not boot, from the
kldload live image.
.Cm import
imports every pool it finds, forced, since a machine that stopped
suddenly never exported them, and without mounting anything over the live
system.
A pool whose devices are zvols is a virtual machine's own disk and is
never imported: two kernels writing one pool destroy it.
Then
.Xr krecovery 8
mounts the installed system, rolls back or repairs the boot loader.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm import
Import each pool found on a disk by id, with
.Fl f
and
.Fl N ;
name each pool skipped for being on a zvol, and each that failed; count
all three.
.It Cm scan
List the importable pools without importing any.
.It Cm list-pools
The imported pools.
.It Cm list-datasets
Their datasets.
.It Cm help , Fl h , Fl -help
Usage; also with no command.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 when a pool did not import or a command failed; 2 for an
unknown command.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop that runs virtual machines, on 2026-09-30, with this
release's
.Nm
first on the path.
.Cm scan
there lists twenty pools named
.Ql tank ,
each on a zvol \(em the guests' own \(em which
.Cm import
skips.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-recovery list-pools
NAME    SIZE  ALLOC   FREE  CKPOINT  EXPANDSZ   FRAG    CAP  DEDUP    HEALTH  ALTROOT
rpool  1.81T  1.61T   207G        -         -    39%    88%  1.00x    ONLINE  -
tank   3.62T  3.31T   327G        -         -     2%    91%  1.00x    ONLINE  -
# (exited 0)
# kldload-recovery frob
Usage:
  kldload-recovery import          import every pool found on a disk, forced, not
                                   mounted (-f -N); pools on zvols are VMs' and
                                   are skipped
  kldload-recovery scan            list importable pools without importing
  kldload-recovery list-pools      list imported pools
  kldload-recovery list-datasets   list datasets of imported pools

For chroot/rollback/bootloader repair, see: krecovery help
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-rollback 8 ,
.Xr krecovery 8 ,
.Xr zpool-import 8
.Sh HISTORY
Until 2026-07-22
.Cm import
only listed the pools and reported success.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: it imported with
.Ql zpool import -a -f ,
which would also force every virtual machine's pool into the host \(em
on the live image, as soon as it was run a second time.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Forcing an import takes a pool another machine still has open.
Only use
.Cm import
where no other machine can reach these disks.
